# Start the API (`dotnet run --project src/Tsundoku.AppHost`, or `dotnet run --project src/Tsundoku.Api`).
# Sign up, follow the confirmation link (Development logs it), then sign in: the calls below use its token.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@email = me@example.test
@password = correct horse battery staple
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Sign up → 202 (the confirmation link is in the log in Development)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Confirm the email → 200 (paste the link from the log: its userId and code)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/confirm-email?userId=PASTE&code=PASTE

### Sign in → 200 { tokenType, accessToken, expiresIn, refreshToken }; unconfirmed → 403; wrong → 401
# @name signIn
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Refresh → 200 with new tokens. Sending the same refresh token again → 401 and the session ends.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{signIn.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

### Who am I → 200 { id, email, emailConfirmed, hasPassword, timezone }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change the time zone (an IANA id) → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/me/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "timezone": "America/Santiago"
}

### Liveness and readiness → 200 (no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists

### Create a list → 201 Created + Location, body is only { id } (CQRS: read it with GET)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries"
}

### Add an item → 201
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Milk"
}

### Complete the item → 204 (a repeated call → 204, nothing changes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/items/{{addItem.response.body.$.id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get the list → 200 (isDone: true, version: 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My lists, newest first → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists?page=1&pageSize=20&search=groc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rename → 204
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Food"
}

### A misspelled property → 400 { code: "bad_request" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "titel": "Groceries"
}

### Delete → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/todo-lists/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### OpenAPI document (Development) — interactive UI at /scalar
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
